  "details": "We all know that Udon Programs in instantiated prefabs are strange... but I've found something related that it's not reported yet.\nIt seems that Udon can't compile correctly if there are no instance of the program while in EditMode.\nI've linked a video showing the issue: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xJpP1QdFbzY\nAs you can see the instanced prefab Udon program do not gets updated (or compiled at all) until I instance the prefab in to the scene while in Edit Mode.\nAfter the prefab is instanced in Edit Mode and you hit Play you can clearly see two different compiled programs running together.\nThe second time you enter PlayMode the prefab instance is updated with the correct version of the compiled Program (Probably, exiting PlayMode will cause some kind of refresh that actually end up updating the prefab instances with the updated program (?))\nSo... that's all, a workaround to ignore this issue until it gets fixed is keeping an instance of the prefab in to the scene ;D",
